  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: Across the three completed experiments, RNA is clearly the dominant signal (rna_only 0.520 vs image_only 0.208), and the only RNA encoder tested so far is scvi_n200. The multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (+1.6%), suggesting that improving the RNA representation could yield a larger absolute gain than tuning the weak image branch. Question: config_023 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is a clean single-variable A/B against config_009, changing only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding profile, model setting, and all other hyperparameters fixed. This isolates the effect of the RNA encoder on the dominant modality. Why this is the best next experiment: With only three data points, the largest source of uncertainty is whether the RNA encoder choice materially affects performance. Resolving this early (i) tells us whether to invest further in scvi_n200-based configurations or pivot to scgpt, (ii) avoids confounding the encoder question with aggregation/fusion/multiprofile variables, and (iii) directly informs the design of all subsequent multimodal experiments where the RNA branch is the primary contributor. A simple rna_only, singleprofile design keeps the experiment interpretable and budget-efficient."
}

